{"toolCallId":"call_97c8af3e8c5d4a08895e61334d6d4d93","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"REPO RULES.md\n---\nFILE_EXISTS error  - Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nPLACEHOLDER_FILLED error  - Rejects unfilled template placeholders in authored spec documents.\nCOMMENT_HYGIENE_MARKER error  - Rejects ephemeral finding markers inside HTML comments in authored spec documents.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED error  - Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nSTATUS_CROSS_DOC_CONSISTENCY error  - Advisory-by-default check that spec.md and implementation-summary.md status fields classify to the same delivery state.\nAC_COVERAGE info  - Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nANCHORS_VALID error  - Checks anchors in each spec doc whose template defines them, ignoring fenced code; a phase parent is exempt, and research/research.md and review/review-report.md are skipped as free-form workflow documents. Errors: a doc with no anchors, an anchor opened twice, never closed, closed but never opened, or closed more times than it is opened. Nesting is also an error: an anchor opened inside another, closed before it is opened, or closed while another is still open, though markers quoted in inline code are ignored by the nesting check; an adr-NNN anchor may hold adr-NNN-* anchors. Template order is not checked.\nSPEC_DOC_SUFFICIENCY error  - Checks implementation-summary sufficiency after save/write flows.\nAI_PROTOCOLS error  - Validates AI execution protocol sections in high-governance specs.\nFOLDER_NAMING error  - Validates numbered spec-folder naming conventions.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID error  - Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nGREP_CONVENTION error  - Checks every markdown document in a spec folder against the greppable-corpus convention: frontmatter variant, trigger phrase quality, anchor grammar and naming.\nLEVEL_MATCH error  - Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_CHILD_DRIFT warn  - Flags graph-metadata.json children_ids missing on-disk phase children the writer would add (advisory unless SPECKIT_CHILD_DRIFT_ENFORCE=true).\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE warn  - Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nMETADATA_DISK_PATH_CONSISTENCY error  - Advisory-by-default check that description.json, graph-metadata.json, and continuity ids match the real on-disk spec-folder path.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE warn  - Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nSPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY error  - Verifies inline markdown references resolve within spec docs.\nTEMPLATE_SOURCE error  - Checks SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE provenance markers.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED error  - Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED error  - Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED error  - Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS error strict - Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nLINKS_VALID warn  - Scans the system-spec-kit skill's own markdown for wikilinks whose target file does not exist. The target is always this skill, never the validated packet.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/wff82223311/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"49da4f","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai